  "body": "Follow-up from the Opus safety review of PR #3857 (fixes #3670), head `ea39d4180`. Non-blocking.\n\n`crates/motion/src/machining3d/reentry.rs:59-63`: the new full-disc gate (a re-entry may plunge only where the whole tool disc is cleared) now also applies to non-centre-cutting tools. A 720-case probe on the `center_cut_law` boss fixture (several tool sizes, stepovers and boss widths) changed 444 of the 600 programs that generate: legal plunges over a cleared core became helix or ramp entries. No new refusals (120 in both runs) and nothing unsafe - the result is only more conservative (longer entries, more air time).\n\nDone means: decide whether a non-centre-cutting tool over a proven-cleared core keeps the plunge (with a pin on the boss fixture), or record that the conservative entry is intended (decision file + pin).\n",
